Cause: the pale lobe is the sweater torso revolve's closed bottom (radius 0 at y 0.72048, ribbed by the cable paint) hanging between the leg tops. Note: the a73bc9a7 12 mm hem drop never moved geometry at all (its cut sat below the closure, so only the rib paint band moved); the lobe predates it. The mockup mom.jpg confirms the intended construction: a straight ribbed hem across the hips with blue jeans directly below.

Fix (assets/sprout-mom.ts): the hem is a true cut at 0.75, above the closure, so the edge is one clean straight line across both hips and the rib band (0.75-0.81) keeps the hem look. A jeans crotch bib (ellipsoid x +-0.10, y 0.66-0.79) fills the leg gap in blue. A blue inner liner (torso wall eroded 2 mm, y 0.68-0.76, same torso weights as the sweater) swallows the kind skin torso bottom, which otherwise shows in the 0.71-0.75 window because the skin wall sits 8 mm inside the sweater but in front of the jeans mass. Liner and sweater share weights, so clearances are constant in every clip. Tucked cones, weighted slimmer hips, side-waist fix, and ef5be6c4 sleeves unchanged. First loop without the liner showed a skin band under the new hem and was corrected in the same turn.

